LibreConvNeXt — third-party attribution
=======================================

The ConvNeXt architecture in this family (``nn.py``) is a native
re-implementation derived from two sources:

    Original code: https://github.com/facebookresearch/ConvNeXt
    Author:        Zhuang Liu et al. (Meta Platforms, Inc.)
    License:       MIT License

    timm reference: https://github.com/huggingface/pytorch-image-models
    File:           timm/models/convnext.py
    Author:         Ross Wightman and the timm contributors
    License:        Apache License 2.0

The block definitions, per-variant depths/dims, the channels-first
``LayerNorm2d``, the layer-scale ``gamma`` parameter, and module/attribute
naming follow timm so that timm's ImageNet-1k pretrained weights load
unchanged and produce bit-identical inference output (verified by the parity
test).

Pretrained weights (convnext_{tiny,small,base}.fb_in1k, ImageNet-1k only —
no extra data, no distillation) are licensed Apache-2.0 in timm and are
redistributable for commercial use.

IMPORTANT — scope: only ConvNeXt **V1** is shipped here. ConvNeXt-V2's small
pretrained checkpoints (atto/femto/pico/nano) are CC-BY-NC 4.0 and are NOT
redistributable in an MIT/commercial library; they are deliberately excluded.

